                <pb facs="0078" n="70" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg70"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.51 Cooperation Program/6a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-06-05T17:00:00-04:00">June 5, 1941—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>138. Conversations have taken place between the Export-Import Bank, the
                    Department and Ambassador Turbay regarding the Colombian request for additional
                    credits. The Bank has already offered to increase the credit to $10,000,000 and
                    the Department continues to press for $12,000,000. The matter should be
                    clarified within a few days.</p>
                <p>The Colombian request included 2 million Colombian pesos for the stabilization
                    fund. The Department, the Export-Import Bank, and the Treasury believe that this
                    is a proper matter for discussion with the Treasury Department, and Ambassador
                    Turbay has been informed of this opinion. He has stated that he would consult
                    his Government for instructions whether to proceed with stabilization
                    discussions with the Treasury Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
